{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For a little while.</b> A short time." "<b>Your holy people inherited.</b> The land, and behold the enemies trampled it. Some say: for a short while, [meaning] those who inherited — \"Your holy people inherited [it]\" — i.e., the inheritors. Or [it means] for a short time, and this is correct."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:50.284778173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}